  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "James",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 4,
    "summary": "Wars are born of lusts—The friends of the world are the enemies of God—Sin is failure to walk in the light we have received.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "From whence come wars and fightings among you? come they not hence, even of your lusts that war in your members?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "TG War."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "GR pleasures, gratifications, passions."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 56
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye lust, and have not: ye kill, and desire to have, and cannot obtain: ye fight and war, yet ye have not, because ye ask not.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye ask, and receive not, because ye ask amiss, that ye may consume it upon your lusts.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Prayer."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "Hel. 10:5 (4–6)."
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "GR wickedly, wrongly. Rom. 8:26 (26–27); D&C 46:30 (28–30); 88:65 (64–65)."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "GR waste, expend. D&C 46:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Lust."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ye adulterers and adulteresses, know ye not that the friendship of the world is enmity with God? whosoever therefore will be a friend of the world is the enemy of God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Whore."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "TG World; Worldliness."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "TG Opposition."
          },
          {
            "start": 154,
            "end": 159,
            "text": "TG Enemies."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Do ye think that the scripture saith in vain, The spirit that dwelleth in us lusteth to envy?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "TG Envy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But he giveth more grace. Wherefore he saith, God resisteth the proud, but giveth grace unto the humble.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Pride."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Poor in Spirit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Reconciliation; Submissiveness."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Abstain; Self-Mastery."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Devil."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "TG God, Presence of."
          },
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Ps. 69:18; D&C 88:63."
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Repent."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 90,
            "text": "TG Purification; Purity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 60
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 70
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 95
          },
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be afflicted, and mourn, and weep: let your laughter be turned to mourning, and your joy to heaviness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "GR Endure hardship, Suffer harassment."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Isa. 22:12; Joel 2:17; 2 Cor. 7:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "TG Mourning."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Contrite Heart; Humility."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Speak not evil one of another, brethren. He that speaketh evil of his brother, and judgeth his brother, speaketh evil of the law, and judgeth the law: but if thou judge the law, thou art not a doer of the law, but a judge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Gossip."
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 128,
            "text": "TG Citizenship."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is one lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy: who art thou that judgest another?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "Morm. 8:20 (19–20)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Go to now, ye that say, To day or to morrow we will go into such a city, and continue there a year, and buy and sell, and get gain:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "Prov. 27:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whereas ye know not what shall be on the morrow. For what is your life? It is even a vapour, that appeareth for a little time, and then vanisheth away.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "1 Cor. 7:31 (29–31); Jacob 7:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For that ye ought to say, If the Lord will, we shall live, and do this, or that.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 17
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But now ye rejoice in your boastings: all such rejoicing is evil.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Boast."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore to him that knoweth to do good, and doeth it not, to him it is sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Luke 12:47; 2 Ne. 9:25 (25–27)."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "TG Disobedience; Good Works; Obedience."
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "TG Sin."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
